# <type>: <short summary, imperative mood, no trailing period>  (≤ 72 chars)
# |<----  Using a max of 72 characters  ---->|

# Body — explain *why*, not *what* (the diff already shows what):
# - what problem this solves, or what would break without it
# - anything a reviewer needs but couldn't infer from the diff

# Types: feat | fix | docs | test | refactor | chore | ci
#
# feat:     a new component, prop, or capability
# fix:      a bug fix
# docs:     documentation only (README, CONTRIBUTING, code comments)
# test:     adding or fixing tests, no production code change
# refactor: no behavior change, no new tests needed
# chore:    tooling, deps, config — nothing that ships to consumers
# ci:       GitHub Actions / workflow changes
#
# Remember to `pnpm changeset` before committing if this change affects
# what gets published to npm — see CONTRIBUTING.md.
